<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <!-- For the Node runtime shipped inside the app (Contents/Resources/node) and for nothing else: the app itself gets none of these.
         Harmless under the ad-hoc signature of local builds; required by the hardened runtime of the Developer ID build (item 4.7,
         scripts/package-mac.sh --release). Why each one is here:

         allow-jit                           V8 compiles JavaScript to machine code at run time and maps that memory with MAP_JIT.
                                             Without it the hardened runtime kills node at its first compile. Needed.
         allow-unsigned-executable-memory    Lets the process make executable memory outside MAP_JIT regions. The official Node build
                                             carries it for V8 and WebAssembly. Kept to match the official build (the release script prints
                                             the official entitlements next to ours). To tighten: remove it, build with --release, and see
                                             whether verify-dmg.sh --release still passes and the hub still boots.
         disable-library-validation          Library validation only lets a process load code signed by Apple or by its own team. The
                                             hub loads better-sqlite3's compiled addon. The release script signs node and the addon with
                                             the same identity, so this should not be needed; it is kept so a native addon that is ever
                                             added with another signer still loads. Same way to tighten as above.

         The agent CLIs (claude, codex, hermes) are separate programs the hub starts. They are not loaded into node, so none of this applies to them. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
